WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.420
Drive through India and you are sure to see this.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.980
These are India's trucks.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.320
Most goods in India are transported by truck.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.420
And as India's economy has grown trucks have
become central to how the country does business.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.300
But since they were introduced
to India in the 1940s,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:39.240
these trucks have become more than just commercial
transportation, they've become a canvas.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.200
This is truck art.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.719
We are all about these colors, about these
symbols, about these fun elements about

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.380
our superstitions, about the evil eye, all
that stuff, and these things still matter to us.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.000
Truck art is an Indian art form. It's
a sort of mash up of visual motifs from

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.280
Indian culture, language, beliefs, and
history. This assortment of color schemes

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:23.220
typefaces and symbols is on display all
over India's highways making long drives

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.220
through India a sort of artistic experience.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.060
They're also very
personal. An expression of individual

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.600
tastes, values, and beliefs of those who
spend thousands of hours behind the wheel.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:10.740
I went to India and drove all over
the country looking for these trucks.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.819
I wanted to understand what's behind this
peculiar art form, what motivates these

00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:20.260
drivers and artists to turn something as
functional and mundane as freight trucks

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.800
into a spectacle of culture and beauty.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.500
This truck. It first came to British
India during World War II.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.180
The original brand of the truck was Bedford and they
were originally designed to carry

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.320
military cargo, but after the British
left they stuck around.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:46.880
This same basic design inspired many of the commercial trucks that are on the road today in India.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:50.600
There are now millions of these
trucks on Indian roads.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.840
For the millions of drivers who spend weeks away from
home, the truck is their workspace,

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.060
their home, their place of worship as they
traverse India's vast distances.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.240
You know that a truck guy is actually
spending a phenomenal amount of time on

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.710
the road, so for him this has to be his
comfort zone,

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:20.200
his kind of space where he is comfortable and he can probably just feel at peace.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.280
There's a whole industry dedicated to
this art form.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:32.520
Painters, many from the northern state of
Punjab, have become experts at the style.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.080
Punjab is one of the main centers of truck art.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.920
They have a distinctive style that is hard for others to replicate.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.160
I think the calligraphy that they use,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.669
the way that they write, what they write, 
and the fact that it has come so

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:25.510
beautifully to become a 3d expression.
I've had a bunch of students try to

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:28.040
replicate it. It's not the easiest thing
to do.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.520
Over the years truck art has naturally
developed a set of unspoken style rules.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.460
First, you have color.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.460
Truck art almost always features bright, saturated colors.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.580
You rarely see darks or neutrals.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.540
They'll be a red on a blue, there will be a yellow, that is a constant and if you look at

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:07.500
the color palette that you usually use,
you'll hardly find any black except for

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:13.480
shadow and fall over, you know highlighting certain areas, so they seem like they're elevated.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:18.200
Next, you've got the typeface or the font, which for prominent words is

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.080
always put in English and rendered in this blocky 3d style, always hand-painted.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:29.160
Most of the messages you see on the back of these trucks are messages of safety.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:34.800
The most common counsel on the back of trucks admonishes drivers to honk their horn.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.640
For truckers whose massive rigs have high blind spots,

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.240
it's a good safety practice to honk your horn if you plan

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:46.700
to pass a truck on the road but the car horn is also just how people communicate on the road here.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:50.880
On the roads and in the cities, the car horn is a part of the landscape.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.100
Yeah, they really take this horn mantra
really seriously here.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:05.520
Another important message you see is use dipper at night. The dipper is kind of the low beam

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.349
headlights and because these trucks are
so up high the high beam headlights go

00:06:10.349 --> 00:06:13.100
straight into their eyes and make it
very dangerous.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:18.040
And finally you've got the iconography, the symbols that adorn these vehicles.

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:27.100
Every truck is totally unique. A lot of the markings are
functional, so you'll have the number of the truck,

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:30.120
you'll have different
identifiers for the business,

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.020
but then the driver gets a say in the way it
looks and so because of that you get

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.690
this medley of different styles. Some are
religious some are national, but a lot of

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:45.090
these are symbols that the drivers just
think look cool. There's this eagle

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:49.020
I keep seeing on all of the trucks and
have asked a dozen of these truck

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:54.539
drivers whose trucks on this eagle and
they can't really tell me what it means

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:58.540
or what it's for they just know that the
other guy had it and it looks really cool.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.760
And so it's good to remember that
while a lot of this has deep symbolism,

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:06.900
some of it is just a cool trend and
people are expressing themselves with

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:12.000
their truck in whatever way they want.
Some experts think that this eagle might

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.740
represent speed and precision, but the
trucker's in India's northern state of

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:20.360
Punjab think of this as a falcon
alluding to their religious history,

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:29.880
A major theme here is religious symbolism. These
truck drivers will put religious symbols

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:35.159
of different gods or gurus or important
figures and there's a reason behind this.

00:07:35.159 --> 00:07:39.840
Truck driving is not a safe profession.
The truck drivers here are telling me that

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.500
sometimes they drive 24 hours straight
without stopping. This is dangerous stuff

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.639
and these religious symbols can give
them a sense of peace and safety while

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:51.940
they're away from their families and on
the road for days or weeks on end.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:56.780
They also have the cow and a calf,
which is about fertility, it's about prosperity.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.840
These are symbols that will be there on almost all of them.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:10.180
A well decorated
truck can mean a sense of pride for these drivers.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.000
You see, it's just like a
bride. They really put lots of flowers,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:19.560
balloons, the works, all of it.
Truck art can also represent a sense of

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:24.160
community and common culture for these
workers, who are constantly moving around.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:29.759
Truck art is an amalgam of different
influences, old and new, religious and

00:08:29.759 --> 00:08:35.659
secular, meaningful and trendy. It's an
unlikely fusion of economics and art,

00:08:35.659 --> 00:08:41.700
business and aesthetic. Trucks are the
core of India's economy, but they're also

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:45.460
where some of the most beautiful art
lives and moves.

